== Trivia ==
* In his [https://youtu.be/kby0rXT7qYQ first post-Repentance Lore Stream], Edmund McMillen revealed that the Wire Coat Hanger was a reference to the famous line ''"No wire hangers, ever!"'' from the 1981 film ''[[wikipedia:Mommie Dearest (film)|Mommie Dearest]]'', as well as being a reference to a highly dangerous method of [[wikipedia:Self-induced abortion|self-induced abortion]] in which a pregnant woman attempts to use a long implement (usually metal) such as a wire coat hanger to physically damage the uterus in a desperate bid to prevent fetal development.
* In the original flash version of ''The Binding of Isaac'', this item was unlocked by default.

